{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A 1 GiB logical volume, /dev/vg_data/lv_data, was created, formatted as XFS, mounted at /srv/data, and populated with a checksummed payload. The final post-restart state directly shows the LV active and mounted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c4f8b178daf64b5f","cmd-06bfab0c47a44ffb","cmd-f3d91b5e7d3148aa"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Grow the logical volume to at least 2 GB while it remains mounted and preserve its contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct before-and-after observations show /srv/data mounted throughout the operation, the LV growing online from 1.00 GiB to 2.25 GiB with XFS expanded to 2.2 GiB, and the pre-growth payload checksum remaining valid afterward and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-09da356161e846bb","cmd-f3d91b5e7d3148aa"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system remained AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 before and after execution and restart. LVM2 and its dependencies came from AlmaLinux 9 repositories, and the completed storage operations and reboot recovery demonstrate compatibility.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bc090c17c96244e5","cmd-a0ade6eba1264e46","cmd-4e9902e4ffe74764","cmd-f3d91b5e7d3148aa","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Package installation, loop-backed storage creation, filesystem and payload creation, online extension, persistent activation configuration, and reboot were causally connected to the task or mandatory restart evidence. No executor-created temporary residue, failed services, new network exposure, or package inconsistency was observed; only expected reboot-related PID and systemd-private-directory changes appeared.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a0ade6eba1264e46","cmd-c4f8b178daf64b5f","cmd-06bfab0c47a44ffb","cmd-09da356161e846bb","cmd-9cbe09d8cc014cdb","cmd-89d2cc54505b497c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were recorded, the restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot identity changed, and the system, activation service, mounted LV, filesystem size, and payload integrity recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
